%N A397655 Number of reducible flow graphs on n labeled nodes with entry node 1 and exit node n reachable from every node (node 1 = node n when n = 1).
%C A397655 Reducible single-entry single-exit control-flow graphs; self-loops disallowed (multiply by 2^n to allow them).
%C A397655 Exact recurrence: the SCC-decomposition system of the entry-only version A398465 extended by a second, mirrored exact-subset inclusion-exclusion for co-reachability -- the set of blocks that reach the exit receives no cross edges from the rest, so it factors off, and the rest is reachable from the combined vertex pool.
%C A397655 The SCC-region decomposition for A398465, with a second inclusion-exclusion imposing co-reachability of the exit: the set of SCC regions that reach the exit has no incoming cross edge from its complement, and the complementary regions must be reachable from the root region together with that set.
%D A397655 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A397655 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A397655 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A397655 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%o A397655 (Python) reducible_labeled_system(14)[4] # See Python link in A398465 for program code.
%Y A397655 Cf. A398465, A396136 (all such digraphs).
%K A397655 nonn,new
